# Everything the build does not need, and two things it must never receive.
#
# `.env` holds a live Anthropic key, a GitHub PAT and the webhook secret. It is
# gitignored, which says nothing about the Docker build context — the build reads
# the working directory, not the index. Excluding it here is what keeps a
# credential out of a layer, and layers are readable by anyone who pulls the
# image even if a later step deletes the file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Untracked internal notes. Same reasoning: gitignore does not filter a build
# context, and this file has already been pushed once by accident.
CLAUDE.md

.git/
.github/
.gitattributes
.gitignore

.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
tests/

# Development-only surfaces. The scripts are the prompt-iteration loop and the
# replay tool; none of them run inside the container.
scripts/
docs/
*.md
!README.md

.idea/
.vscode/
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
